sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant U as Player / Operator / Host
    participant R as Web app routing
    participant UI as UI rendering
    participant SA as Scoring actions
    participant MS as Match sync
    participant FL as Firebase repositories
    participant D as Hub / Beacon / Pulse
    participant I as postEvent
    participant F as Firestore
    participant T as onEventCreate
    participant G as Scoring / Replay
    participant K as manageMatch
    participant Q as manageTournament
    participant O as Overlay / read client
    participant A as Public API

    opt Open a court (/c/{courtId} or /p/{courtId})
        U->>R: Navigate or follow a court link
        R->>FL: Read court document
        FL->>K: ensureCourtMatch when needed
        K->>F: Create or return live match
        R->>MS: Follow courts/{courtId}.activeMatchId
        MS->>FL: Attach match + score listeners
        R->>UI: Show scoreboard with match title primary
    end

    opt Open match or tournament
        U->>R: Navigate to /m/{matchId} or /t/{tournamentId}
        R->>FL: Read match, score or tournament read model
        R->>UI: Render match page, public dashboard or host control room
    end

    alt Browser scoring action
        U->>UI: Score / undo in app
        UI->>SA: addPoint / undoLastPoint
        SA->>UI: Immediate animation + sound feedback
        SA->>FL: Add match event
        FL->>F: Write matches/{matchId}/events/{eventId}
    else Physical device action
        U->>D: Physical action
        D->>I: POST /postEvent
        I->>F: Resolve device binding and court activeMatchId
        I->>K: ensureCourtMatch if the court has no live match
        I->>I: Apply beaconSidesSwapped for Beacon events
        I->>F: Append matches/{matchId}/events/{eventId}
    end

    F-->>T: Match event document created
    T->>F: Read match + event + current score
    T->>T: Check scoreVersion and event ordering

    alt Out-of-order event or UNDO
        T->>G: Full match-history replay
    else Normal scoring
        T->>G: Apply event / checkpoint
    end

    G-->>T: Materialized score
    T->>F: Write matches/{matchId}/score/current
    T->>F: Write checkpoint when required
    T->>F: Update match scoreSummary/result
    opt Tournament fixed-end match completes
        T->>Q: tournament hook after match change
        Q->>F: Update fixture result, standings, bracket and read models
    end
    F-->>MS: Match score snapshot
    MS->>UI: Render points, games, sets, server, fixed-total state and badges

    opt Public scoreboard or overlay
        O->>A: GET /revision/{courtId} or /revision/match/{matchId}
        A->>F: Resolve court or match target
        A-->>O: Revision payload

        O->>A: GET /score/{courtId} or /score/match/{matchId}
        A->>F: Read match and current score
        A-->>O: Live score payload with match context
    end

    opt Tournament host operation
        U->>UI: Generate round, assign court, correct result, complete tournament
        UI->>Q: manageTournament with host/admin credentials
        Q->>F: Transactional tournament/match/read-model writes
        F-->>UI: Updated read model
    end

    opt Match move / reset / completion
        UI->>K: manageMatch operation
        K->>F: Transactional court + match writes
        K->>F: Reset archives match events and increments scoreVersion when requested
    end

    Note over I,D: Current device identity is deviceId/binding. HMAC, freshness, replay protection and idempotency are production targets.
    Note over K,Q,F: Host keys are hashed; admin skeleton key is verified server-side. Legacy court/device rules remain development-open.
    Note over F: Match events are authoritative. Current score and tournament views are derived state.
